# Own-wording spells of Dark Matter (2014 rules), part A. TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
HL = "\n\n**At Higher Levels.** "
TEXT = {
"Abduct": ["100 miles, 1 hour. Pull a creature whose location you know to a spot within 30 ft of you. An unwilling target makes a Charisma save.",
 "100 miles, 1 hour. Teleport a creature within range to you. An unwilling creature makes a Charisma save to resist. You must know its exact location. If it is more than 100 ft from where you think it is, it has Advantage on the save. If it is more than 500 ft off, the spell fails. On a failed save the target appears at a spot you choose within 30 ft of you, and you decide whether it sits, stands, lies prone or is bound by nearby restraints. When the spell ends you decide whether it stays or returns to where it was taken from."],
"Antivirus": ["Touch, 24 hours. A device cannot be disabled by magic or infected by the N-Virus, and hackers have Disadvantage against it.",
 "Touch, 24 hours. You ward a device from digital intruders. For the duration it cannot be disabled by magical effects such as technical difficulties or logic bomb, and it cannot be infected by the N-Virus. Creatures have Disadvantage on Intelligence (Data) checks to hack it."],
"Arcane Anomaly": ["30 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. Each spell cast within range has a 1 in 6 chance to fail.",
 "30 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You crack the magical energy around you. For the duration, whenever a spell is cast within range, roll a d6. On a 1 the casting fails. The slot is spent as normal, but expensive material components are not consumed."],
"Arcane Capacitor": ["Touch. Melee spell attack for 5d10 Force damage, then regain an expended 1st-level slot.",
 "Touch. You channel arcane power through your fingertips and recycle the leftover energy. Make a melee spell attack against a creature you can reach. On a hit it takes 5d10 Force damage. Hit or miss, you then regain one expended 1st-level spell slot." + HL + "If you cast it with a 7th-level slot, you regain a 2nd-level slot instead. With a 9th-level slot, you regain a 3rd-level slot."],
"Asteroid Cluster": ["20,000 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. A 2,000 ft cube slows ships and mega creatures and damages them for 2d8 mega Bludgeoning.",
 "20,000 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You create a cluster of asteroids that fills a 2,000-ft cube. Each ship and mega creature inside is slowed: each foot of movement costs one extra foot. A mega creature or ship in the cluster that did not take Evasive Maneuvers takes 2d8 mega Bludgeoning damage at the start of its turn. An attack made through the cluster treats the target as having half cover." + HL + "With a slot of 3rd level or higher, the cube grows by 500 ft and the damage rises by 1d8 mega for each slot level above 2nd."],
"Astrogation": ["Self, 1 minute, Concentration. A void jump made during the spell is a perfect jump.",
 "Self, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You burn rare spices and incense worth at least 100 gp, which the spell consumes, to briefly find your course through the universe. If you perform a void jump while the spell lasts, you automatically make a perfect jump."],
"Autopilot": ["Touch, 1 hour. A ship makes pilot, engineer and gunner checks for itself and can fly a set course.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. You give a spaceship a limited ability to run without its crew. For the duration it can make the ability checks and saves its pilot, engineer or gunner would make, even if nobody holds the role. Treat its ability scores as 10 with no proficiencies. When you cast it you can choose a speed and direction within the ship's cone of movement for the ship to follow when no creature is in the Pilot role. It moves automatically at the start of the initiative order, and this stops when a creature enters the Pilot role. The ship cannot be commandeered while the spell lasts." + HL + "With a slot of 3rd level or higher, the duration is 8 hours."],
"Cheat": ["Self, 1 round. Reroll any ability check for a nonmagical game of skill.",
 "Self, 1 round. You twist your fingers and fate follows. For the duration you can reroll any ability check you make to play nonmagical games of skill. It could sway a game of poker, but not a Deck of Many Things."],
"Circuit Breaker": ["5 ft. Dexterity save or 3d8 Lightning damage to nearby creatures, and magical technology is disabled.",
 "Reaction when you are damaged by a creature within 5 ft that you see. You release a burst of electricity. Each creature within 5 ft makes a Dexterity save or takes 3d8 Lightning damage, or half on a success. Each piece of magical technology in range is also disabled until the end of your next turn." + HL + "The damage rises by 1d8 for each slot level above 2nd."],
"Comet Strike": ["15,000 ft. A comet hits a target for 4d10 mega Bludgeoning and 4d10 mega Cold. Dexterity save for half.",
 "15,000 ft. You create a chunk of rock and ice that strikes a target in range. The target, or the pilot if the target is a ship, makes a Dexterity save. If it is a ship with no one in the Pilot role, the save automatically fails. On a failure the target takes 4d10 mega Bludgeoning and 4d10 mega Cold damage, or half as much on a success." + HL + "With a slot of 6th level or higher, the Cold damage rises by 1d10 mega for each slot level above 5th."],
"Commandeer Weapon": ["5,000 ft, Concentration. Take over a ship weapon on a failed Constitution save by the gunner.",
 "5,000 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. Choose a ship weapon mounted on a spaceship you see. A gunner operating it makes a Constitution save. If nobody controls it, the save automatically fails. On a failure you control the weapon for the duration and can fire it with your action as if you were a gunner, and no gunner on the target ship can fire it. A gunner controlling the weapon at the end of their turn can repeat the save to end the effect."],
"Conjure Hardlight Avatar": ["90 ft, 15 hours, Concentration. Summon a hardlight etherolus or juggernautus that follows your commands.",
 "90 ft, up to 15 hours, Concentration. You call into being a sophisticated hardlight construct of gears, pistons and plates. A hardlight etherolus or hardlight juggernautus appears in an unoccupied space in range. It disappears at 0 hit points or when the spell ends. It rolls its own initiative and takes its own turns. As a bonus action you can mentally command it while it is within 500 ft. You choose its action and movement, or give a general command such as guarding a corridor. Without commands it only defends itself. Magic cannot restore its hit points, because hardlight evaporates."],
"Conjure Nebula": ["5,000 ft, up to 15 hours, Concentration. A 1,000 ft sphere of gas and dust heavily obscures the area.",
 "5,000 ft, up to 15 hours, Concentration. You create a sphere of gas and dust with a 1,000-ft radius centered on a point in range. The area is heavily obscured." + HL + "With a slot of 2nd level or higher, the radius rises by 1,000 ft for each slot level above 1st."],
"Create Vacuum": ["60 ft, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. A sphere up to 30 ft in radius with almost no air. Air breathers suffocate.",
 "60 ft, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. You create a sphere nearly empty of air, centered on a point in range. You choose a radius up to 30 ft. Any air-breathing creature inside must hold its breath or begin suffocating. If the point is on an object you hold, or one that is not worn or carried, the sphere centers on the object and moves with it. Airborne substances such as poison gas, smoke or fog cannot enter it, and those inside are destroyed. A substance created by a spell of higher level than this one is unaffected."],
"Cryptogram": ["Unlimited. Send a scroll with an 8-character message to a known creature on your plane, once a day per target.",
 "Unlimited. You send a small scroll with a short message to a creature of your choice. The recipient must be known to you and on your plane. The scroll hovers before it, drops into its pocket or appears on something nearby. The message holds up to 8 characters, spaces included. You can send only one scroll a day to a single target."],
"Dark Anchor": ["5,000 ft, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. A ship cannot begin a void jump if its engineer fails a Wisdom save.",
 "5,000 ft, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. Choose a spaceship you see in range. Its engineer makes a Wisdom save, and the save automatically fails if no one holds the role. On a failure the ship cannot start a void jump for the duration. A jump already initiated cannot begin until the spell ends. An engineer at their station who is not incapacitated can repeat the save at the end of each of their turns, ending the effect on a success."],
"Delay": ["60 ft. Wisdom save or the target drops to last in initiative from the next round.",
 "60 ft. You briefly slow time for a creature you see in range. The target must succeed on a Wisdom save or be moved to last place in the initiative order from the start of the next round onward."],
"Destruct": ["1,000 ft. Spell attack against a ship for 10d20 + 40 mega Force damage.",
 "1,000 ft. You bring all your magic to bear and unleash a wave of destructive energy at a ship. Make a spell attack roll against a ship you see in range. On a hit it takes 10d20 + 40 mega Force damage."],
"Dire Mutation": ["10 ft. Constitution save or a Large or smaller beast becomes a hulking monstrosity with +40 HP, +2 AC and double size.",
 "10 ft. You scramble the genetics of a Large or smaller beast, or a summoned creature shaped like one, in range. An unwilling beast makes a Constitution save. The spell has no effect on shapechangers or creatures transformed by magic. On a failure the beast becomes a monstrosity and changes as follows: its current and maximum hit points rise by 40; its AC rises by 2; its size doubles in every dimension, its weight is multiplied by eight, and it is one size category larger; it gains Multiattack with two melee weapon attacks, or one extra attack if it has it; its attacks can use your spell attack bonus if higher than its own; it is hostile to you and your companions unless you summoned it. The spell ends and the target reverts if it drops to 0 hit points. When it ends, its hit points return to what they were before the change."],
"Disruption Field": ["5,000 ft, Concentration. A ship's shield generator is disabled if its engineer fails a Wisdom save.",
 "5,000 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You disrupt the energy around a ship you see in range. Its engineer makes a Wisdom save, and the save automatically fails if no one holds the role. On a failure the ship's shield generator is disabled for the duration. An engineer who is not incapacitated can repeat the save at the end of each of their turns, ending the effect on a success."],
"Earth-Shattering Kaboom": ["120 ft. A 30 ft blast of 5d8 Thunder and 5d8 Radiant, Dexterity save for half.",
 "120 ft, 1 round. Streams of arcane energy gather into an unstable ball at a point you see in range. When the spell ends, at its peak, you rupture the ball in a massive detonation. Roll a d20. On a 1 the ball fizzles. On any other result each creature in a 30-ft-radius sphere centered on the point makes a Dexterity save, taking 5d8 Thunder and 5d8 Radiant damage on a failure, or half on a success." + HL + "With a slot of 5th level or higher, the Thunder or Radiant damage (your choice) rises by 1d8 for each slot level above 4th."],
}
